{"id": "EUVD-2026-101741", "enisaUuid": "5b333916-2b7f-3b6f-aa43-955ff8d7835b", "description": "GitPython from 3.1.30 before 3.2.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability in Remote.pull() whose unsafe-option guard inspects only keyword arguments, not the positional refspec. Attackers controlling the refspec can supply --upload-pack=<command> to execute OS commands as the calling process over local-path or SSH transports.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:14:41", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-f9j4-qggq-h239", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-3.1.30-before-3.2.0-command-injection-via-remote-pull-refspec"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mcf4-6385-6rcq", "CVE-2026-110858"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "88b572be-f01b-3e0b-aa02-ac3cd2f7d8c2", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "3.1.30 <3.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c51f11ea-cd2b-3e12-b22b-61e9735a06b8", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}